# Open content

Replacement content that lets the engine run without the original game:
the original's first area, walked on like the original's with our own walls
and trees (Remote Town, Cold Svalt Town and the fields, forests and dungeons
round them), the hero and the heroine with their equipment, the title screen (`System/Title/Pattern/Title`, stone and copper pipes rendered in Blender by `tools/art/title_screen.py`, the name set in New Rocker under the SIL Open Font License 1.1) and the steam blowing from its pipes (`Smoke00-09`, painted by `tools/art/title_smoke.py`), the Create New Character screen (`System/Select`, drawn by `tools/art/select_screen.py` with figures from `tools/art/portraits.py`), 24 kinds of monster, the
townspeople, the hero's dogs (`partners.txt`, `Character/PARTNER`, with the dash's speed streak painted by `tools/art/streak.py`), items, the game panel along the bottom of the screen (`tools/art/panel.py`) and the magic bar's icons (`tools/art/magic_icons.py`), the inventory panel, the shop window, the GATE window (`tools/art/warp.py`), the card game and the Change Color window (`System/Game/Pattern/Card` and `ChangeColor`, drawn by `tools/art/cards.py`), the speech
balloon, the font, the spell, trap and script effects (`Character/OPTION`,
painted by `tools/art/effects.py`) and the story pages that open and close
each episode (`System/Common/Pattern/Visual01`-`06`, `Waiting` and
`WaitIcon`, painted by `tools/art/story.py`; the story is told in our own
words and set in Liberation Serif Italic, under the SIL Open Font License
1.1), and the sound effects and music (`System/Game/Voice`,
`System/Game/Music` and `System/Title/Music`, synthesized and composed by
`tools/sound`). The formats are described in
[docs/content.md](../docs/content.md).

All of it is made for this project: modelled and rendered in Blender by
the scripts in [tools/art](../tools/art) and laid out by
`tools/art/build_pack.py`, in the style of the original game but drawn
from scratch, with no original pictures traced or reused. The sounds are
made the same way: synthesized by our own scripts, with no recording of
the original's sampled or reused, and the music is our own. The monsters'
behaviour and drop lists (`ai.txt`) are ours, but the numbers in the
monster stats, the item definitions (`items.txt`) and the dogs' stats
(`partners.txt`) are the original's, copied by the scripts in
`tools/content`; the names and wording are ours.

The unique weapons' pictures (`System/Game/Pattern/Item0002` and
`Character/ITEM/00000009`) build their swords, axes, hammers and crossbow
prods on Quaternius's Medieval Weapons Pack (CC0, public domain; kept in
[tools/art/quaternius](../tools/art/quaternius)), repainted and reshaped
per item by `tools/art/uniques.py`.
The plain swords in `System/Game/Pattern/Item0004` (pictures drawn to stand
in for the original's items, by `tools/art/item_extras.py`) are built on
the same models.

## License

Everything in this folder is under the MIT license, the same as the
engine's code; see [LICENSE](../LICENSE) at the top of the repository.
# generated by tools/content/first_area.py after the original's scenario 0
title=Remote Town
map=f00_01
entry=0,4138,8251,3
entry=50,8925,2684,7
entry=100,6563,7856,7
town=10000000
exit=4258,9781,5328,10319,10000001,0
person=13,5707,6972,7,commander
person=8,2780,6719,1,smith
person=9,4285,5394,0,healer
person=1000000,3634,2085,1,ash
person=1000000,4035,2475,1,soot
person=1000000,4051,1838,7,amber
person=1000001,1402,8366,1,pip
# Remote Town's people: where every new game begins, as in the original
# (scenario 0). The talk follows the original's order, purposes and
# flags in our own words:
#
# - the commander greets the hero over several boxes and hands over the
#   army's kit and a little gold (save:4 met him); below level 5 he has
#   nothing more; from level 5, once the beast to the north-east is
#   dealt with (quest:0 cleared), he sends the hero to clear the Dusty
#   Ruins (quest:3); when that is done he pays 1500 gold (save:2) and
#   sends the hero west through the Wasteland of Pillars to Cold Svalt.
# - the smith keeps the shop: sour (save:9 heard his complaint) until the
#   beast is dead, then warms up (save:6 1, then 2 once he says so) and
#   asks for his stolen gem back (quest:1); for it he tells of an exiled
#   trader in the Wasteland of Pillars. Once the ruins are clear and the
#   commander has sent the hero on, he gives a parting gift (save:8); he
#   hands over the old knight's order for quest:5 (save:21); once the
#   first area is finished (save:71) he sells only potions (save:70).
#   Otherwise he trades, identifies and repairs.
# - the healer gives the first mission (quest:0), later the shrine stone
#   (quest:2, once quest:3 is taken and the hero is past level 5), thanks
#   the hero for it and gives a parting gift (save:7); otherwise she heals
#   the hero when hurt.
#
# Each person keeps which of their boxes is showing in a TEMP flag (the
# commander temp:2, the smith temp:11, the healer temp:21) so that
# closing it shows the next. As IF runs its sentence and carries on, each
# talk-end sentence first copies that flag, and each check comes before
# the sentence that would make it true.
#
# The warp gate north-east of the square, as the original's: walking up
# to it finds it (warp:0, which a new game already has) and shows its
# name over it, and a click on it opens the GATE window.

object=9361,2086,9658,2337,gate
# The ground round it is a judge area only: unusable, as the original's, so
# a held click on the square still walks.
object=8160,697,10460,3197,gate-ground,states=0/0/0
object=6261,5738,6872,6355,warehouse,warehouse

# The healer's blessing (temp:26) starts with none said yet.
temp=26,-1

# The shop's stock: tools only once the first area is finished.
[sentence town-start]
on=start
IF save:71 = 0 @stock-all
IF save:71 ! 0 @stock-tools
GETENTRYPOINT temp:5
IF temp:5 = 50 @arrive-by-gate

[sentence stock-all]
INITTRADE 0 0

[sentence stock-tools]
INITTRADE 0 22

[sentence arrive-by-gate]
PLAYSOUND 53 0 x:gate y:gate

[sentence warehouse]
on=talk warehouse
STORAGE 0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- commander

[message 1]
So the army did send someone. I command what is left of the
garrison in this town, which is not much.

Goblins and worse prowl along our wall every night.
I have not slept well in weeks.

[message 2]
There is no money for more soldiers, and sooner or later the
town will fall unless something changes. Most townsfolk have
gone. A few traders and the shrine's healer stayed.

So we make do with the handful of us there are.

[message 3]
Start with the goblins around the town. There are plenty,
but they have no leader. Think of it as training.

[message 4]
Here, kit from the army stores, and some coin to go with it.
It is not much, but it is all we were given.

Put it on in your bag before you go out there.

[message 5]
Come and see me when you can. If I hear anything new,
you will be the first to know.

[message 6]
Nothing new to tell you yet.
Keep at what you were sent to do.

[message 7]
Grow strong enough to take up a proper fighting trade,
and I will have harder work for you.

[message 8]
A patrol came back from the Dusty Ruins, far to the
north-west. The goblins have been moving in there and
making the place their stronghold.

[message 9]
You have bought us some breathing room here. Go to the ruins
and root out whoever leads them.

[message 10]
One more thing: there is a warp gate near the ruins.
Find it and it will save you the long walk back.

[message 11]
I am counting on you. Off to the ruins.

[message 12]
You did it. For the first time in months this town is safe.

Here is your pay. You have earned every coin.

[message 13]
Now there is trouble at Cold Svalt Town: monsters are at
its gates. Go west through the Wasteland of Pillars and
you will reach it.

