[message 1000000]
Kanfore, Mining Town

[message 1000001]
Kanfore, Mining Town

[message 1000002]
So you're the one they sent. Good.
Name's Harlan. This operation is mine
to run.

[message 1000003]
I give the orders, but the fighting I leave
to people like you. Bring me results;
that's all I ask.

[message 1000004]
The man over there is Tobin, my second.
Take your questions to him.

[message 1000005]
Let's not waste time. Here's your first job.

[message 1000006]
Everything this operation needs is stored here,
and a band of thieves out of the demon army wants it.
They hide in the Forest of Claws, south-east of town.
Break that band before anything else.

[message 1000007]
Bring down the ones who lead them, and the rest
should fall apart. Aim for the leaders.

[message 1000008]
When it's done, report back to me.
Off you go.

[message 1000009]
Hired swords come in every kind. Some are worth
more than a knight. Knights look the part,
but there's often little behind the armor.

[message 1000010]
Well done.
Your pay first. Here.

[message 1000011]
Next, I need a mining tunnel looked at. The operation
depends on it, and it lies a long way south of here.

[message 1000012]
The way there runs through the elves' forest. I'm still
asking them to let you through; until they agree,
get past as quietly as you can.

[message 1000013]
Luck go with you.

[message 1000014]
I hardly believe it...
The dragon of the old stories, slain?

[message 1000015]
I never expected that much of you...

[message 1000016]
While fighters like you still walk the land,
these dark days are not hopeless.

[message 1000017]
Maybe I'm looking at a true hero.

[message 1000018]
Whatever stands in your way, you'll get past it.
I'm sure of that now.

[message 1000019]
Keep our hopes alive.

[message 1000020]
The elves wouldn't let you through their forest?
Then the talks are going badly.

[message 1000021]
I think it's the dragon from the old tales
that has them worried.

[message 1000022]
They say it sleeps somewhere in a mine, shut in
long ago behind a wizard's shield of magic...

[message 1000023]
It's still young, but even so it once had the strength
to drown a whole kingdom in fire.

[message 1000024]
The elves live in fear
of it waking.

[message 1000025]
If our army goes through that tunnel as it pleases,
it could disturb the seal and wake the beast.
That's what the elves are afraid of.

[message 1000026]
They take this very seriously,
it seems.

[message 1000027]
We need someone who knows the seal well to vouch for us,
someone who can talk the elves round...

[message 1000028]
The dragon was sealed by a well-known wizard, Orsolan.
His tower stands deep in the Forest of Spirits,
east of Cross Agora.

[message 1000029]
Go to him. Ask him to help us
win the elves over.

[message 1000030]
Marsh fever has been going round the town lately.

[message 1000031]
The war held up the rebuilding of the Marsh Quarter.
The place is filthy, and the fever was born there
and spread from it.

[message 1000032]
With the elven remedy it's seldom deadly...

[message 1000033]
...but the remedy has run short.

[message 1000034]
It's made from herbs grown in a garden that Morrow
the merchant keeps. We can't get any more of it.
A bad year, he says.

[message 1000035]
And that greedy merchant named a price for more of it
that no one could pay.

[message 1000036]
We don't trust the way he does business,
but we can't go in there and look.

[message 1000037]
The garden is on elven land. Make trouble there
and the operation could be held up.

[message 1000038]
I'm told an elf leader gave Morrow the garden to keep,
as a sign of goodwill between our peoples.

[message 1000039]
Morrow's dealings make my blood boil,
but for now my hands are tied.

[message 1000040]
I'm sorry. On the matter of the herb garden,
we can't help you.

[message 1000041]
I heard what you did about the herb garden. Hard work,
and it paid off: the army has all the remedy it needs.

[message 1000042]
You're better than the stories about you.
We'll lean on you gladly from here on.

[message 1000043]
Sella can go on as before. The Guild agreed to it,
seeing as this was no ordinary case.

[message 1000044]
Hello. I'm Tobin; I help run this operation.
Glad to have you.

[message 1000045]
Above all, we need the road clear,
so the army can strike before the enemy knows.

[message 1000046]
An old mine tunnel is to be our way through.
I want you to look it over
and make it safe.

[message 1000047]
There's also a band of thieves round here,
and they've proved tougher than we
reckoned on.

[message 1000048]
They fight well. Deserters from the demon army
pulled them together.

[message 1000049]
We haven't confirmed it, but some of the demons'
senior officers may be among them.

[message 1000050]
Why they keep going after our supplies,
we don't know. But we can't lose
any more time over them.

[message 1000051]
They've also cornered some of our allies. We won't leave
anyone to them. Go and see what you can find. Good luck.

[message 1000052]
Keep at it.

[message 1000053]
Well. That's... impressive. I wouldn't have tried it.
Never mind me.

[message 1000054]
I expect nothing short of success.
Good luck!

[message 1000055]
Ever since the fever spread, the remedy has been scarce.
Sella, the spirit healer, buys it herself
and gives it to the poor.

[message 1000056]
Good of her.

[message 1000057]
Not that it's any business of mine.

[message 1000058]
She charges for her healing?
Well, it makes sense. She paid for the remedy.

[message 1000059]
Charging without the Guild's leave is against the rules,
and she does it. But she means no harm by it.

[message 1000060]
I'll keep it to myself for now.
If word got out, she'd be in real trouble...

[message 1000061]
Anyway, it's nothing to do with me.

[message 1000062]
The remedy costs far more now?
Probably a poor harvest
of the herbs.

[message 1000063]
There's ugly talk about the man who supplies it,
but who can blame someone for wanting a profit?

[message 1000064]
Venn did much the same, didn't he? Bought up
the town's remedy and made a fat
profit on it.

[message 1000065]
Had I the means, I'd be rich by now too...
Not that it's my concern.

[message 1000066]
If I get impatient, this fight is lost.
(sigh)

[message 1000067]
About these doubts over Morrow... fixing the price
of the remedy, buying off the inspectors... I can't say
I care. But people's lives hang on it,
and that does trouble me.

[message 1000068]
What? You think I should be angry?
Go against the people above me?

[message 1000069]
It makes no difference. No one asks what I think...
It has nothing to do with me...

[message 1000070]
Please don't ask someone with nothing to do with it
questions that only make things awkward...

[message 1000071]
Oh, you're wonderful. I always knew you'd do it.
Truly!

[message 1000072]
Ha ha ha...

[message 1000073]
This war has made me a rich man.
I can't stop laughing! Ha ha ha!

[message 1000074]
Oops. Forget I said that.
Ha ha ha!

[message 1000075]
Time to spend some of it. What shall we try next?
Ha ha ha!

[message 1000076]
The remedy's too dear, you think? Nothing I can do
about that. The price follows the demand.

[message 1000077]
Take it up with Morrow if you don't like it...
Oops. You didn't hear that!

[message 1000078]
What of it? My business is honest.
What others do is no affair of mine!

[message 1000079]
I told you, I know nothing about Morrow!
.......

[message 1000080]
Don't look at me like that.
I know nothing about it.

[message 1000081]
........ngh.

[message 1000082]
.....hngh.

[message 1000083]
..Wh

[message 1000084]
Stop that.

[message 1000085]
Stop smiling at me like that.

[message 1000086]
Fine! I'll tell you everything!
And why are you glowing like that!?

[message 1000087]
Hm..

[message 1000088]
Word is that Morrow has been raising the remedy's price on his
own, without asking anyone, while the elves' leader is away.

[message 1000089]
We did well out of this war, trading goods and supplies.
The elven remedy is wanted everywhere. However much
of it we sell, people want more.

[message 1000090]
Morrow kept a stock of the remedy hidden. When the price
went up, he sold it on the quiet to whoever paid most.
Think what that brought him.

[message 1000091]
That's why the market ran dry. He must have found
a buyer with deep pockets. The fighting at the front
is harder now, all because of him.

[message 1000092]
Everyone blames him, but nothing can be done:
the inspectors say there's nothing wrong.

[message 1000093]
Put simply, the inspectors are in his pocket.
They're part of the whole rotten business.

[message 1000094]
That's all I'm telling you.

[message 1000095]
That's enough, isn't it?
Stop staring at me!

[message 1000096]
I asked about Morrow..
and got a real dressing-down!
We're finished talking..

[message 1000097]
Please, forgive me!
I've done nothing wrong!

[message 1000098]
What can I do for you?

  ~Buy weapons           ~
  ~Buy gear              ~
  ~Identify items        ~
  ~Repair items          ~
                              ~Leave~

[message 1000099]
  ~Weapon             %9d Gold~
  ~Helmet             %9d Gold~
  ~Body armor         %9d Gold~
  ~Shield             %9d Gold~
  ~Boots              %9d Gold~
  ~Everything worn    %9d Gold~
  ~Everything carried %9d Gold~
                          ~Leave~

[message 1000100]
You can't afford that.

[message 1000101]
Nothing here needs mending.

[message 1000102]
Identifying that comes to %d Gold. All right?

                         ~Yes~  ~No~

[message 1000103]
There's nothing unknown here.

[message 1000104]
I'm Sella.
They sent me here not long ago.
Pleased to meet you.

[message 1000105]
The army pays you well, I hear?
Then I'm afraid healing will cost you.

[message 1000106]
How are you keeping?

[message 1000107]
If you want healing, you'll need to pay.

[message 1000108]
Charging for healing is against the rules?
I thought you'd say that!

[message 1000109]
Complain to your officers if you like.
Let the Guild throw me out. I don't care!

[message 1000110]
..That greedy man! Doesn't he care who lives or dies?

[message 1000111]
Oh! Forgive me!
I was miles away..

[message 1000112]
If you're hurt, I'll heal you right away.. no, wait, I didn't say that!
Pay for your treatment!

[message 1000113]
What? Don't look at me like that.
You don't like that I charge?

[message 1000114]
I don't care. If you don't like it,
find someone else to heal you!

[message 1000115]
So what?
I don't want to take your money, but...

[message 1000116]
........

[message 1000117]
The remedy is dear. I have to charge.

[message 1000118]
Anything else to complain about?

[message 1000119]
Thank you, for everything.
I'm grateful, truly...
I expect the healers will dismiss me in the end.
Until then I'll heal you for nothing,
so do come by...

[message 1000120]
Healing wounds is all I can do.
I'm sorry...

[message 1000121]
How are things?

[message 1000122]
The townsfolk pleaded with the healers
not to dismiss me....

[message 1000123]
.....

[message 1000124]
So I can go on
healing you after all.

[message 1000125]
That's all I wanted to tell you.

[message 1000126]
You aren't hurt.

[message 1000127]
Healing is 200 Gold. Is that all right?

                    ~Yes~  ~No~

[message 1000128]
You aren't hurt.
Look after yourself...

[message 1000129]
Come back if you need me.

[message 1000130]
Spirits, mend these wounds.

[message 1000131]
Spirits!
Take this pain away.

[message 1000132]
I'm sorry. You haven't enough money.

[message 1000133]
How are you keeping?

[message 1000134]
Hello there!
Welcome to Kanfore, the mining town!

[message 1000135]
Between ourselves, the army's made this place
lively of late!

[message 1000136]
Since they put their camp here,
we've been doing very nicely!

[message 1000137]
There's a nasty fever about.
Take care of yourself.

[message 1000138]
Let's make our fortunes and spend them right here.
We'll have a fine time of it!

[message 1000139]
Hey, you. See that spirit healer over there?
Pretty face, but she makes you pay. Imagine that!

[message 1000140]
I took a fall and couldn't get up,
and she wanted 3 gold out of me!
The greedy thing!

[message 1000141]
I was so cross I beat her down to 1 gold.
She said that wouldn't even pay for the remedy.
Nonsense, if you ask me!

[message 1000142]
When I was a boy, healers never asked a penny.
What's happened to the world?!

[message 1000143]
She acts all kind,
but it's the money she's after...

[message 1000144]
What? She broke the rules and risked her place
to buy the remedy for everyone?

[message 1000145]
I'd never have guessed!
It's been years since I met someone that good!

[message 1000146]
Who puts anything ahead of money, after all?
That's too good to be true.

[message 1000147]
Oh...
Should I go and say goodbye to him?

[message 1000148]
He never does a day's work.
I only heal for free those who work hard!

[message 1000149]
Folk who don't pay their dues should be grateful
I heal them so cheaply.

[message 1000150]
Other healers charge far more for this.
He doesn't see that...

[message 1000151]
That girl never used to charge for healing.
What's got into her?
Has some smooth-talker led her astray?

[message 1000152]
.....

[message 1000153]
I feel for her.
Her life can't have been easy.
Those who sneer at her should be ashamed.

[message 1000154]
Well, no point being careful now.
I've caught the marsh fever.

[message 1000155]
It's named for the Marsh Quarter, where it started.
It spreads like nothing else, but with the remedy
it's not too bad..

[message 1000156]
(cough)
I'm strong, I'll pull through,
but the weaker folk...

[message 1000157]
It spread so fast and got so bad..
Nothing stopped it until the remedy was found.

[message 1000158]
I'll live, for Posy's sake.. I'll be fine..

[message 1000159]
I can't die before my girl
can make her own way.

[message 1000160]
.....(cough!)

[message 1000161]
Sella, over there, always brings me remedy.
She says not to worry about taking it,
since it comes from the Guild's store for the town.
But something about it feels wrong..

[message 1000162]
Oh, there you are!
Thanks to you, there's remedy enough again,
and everyone's well!

[message 1000163]
I'm grateful to Sella too.
I've heard she wasn't allowed
to charge for healing...

[message 1000164]
I never knew she'd put her own work at risk
to buy the remedy and hand it out.

[message 1000165]
We're getting up a petition for her.
I think it'll go through!
It's our turn to help her.

[message 1000166]
You've done so much for us. Thank you.
You'll always have friends here.

[message 1000167]
Dad... if only he had the elven remedy,
he'd get better soon...

[message 1000168]
Why does the remedy keep costing more?
We can't pay that much.

[message 1000169]
Others are in the same state. Without the remedy
Sella gives us, no one would pull through..

[message 1000170]
Sella hasn't looked well herself lately..
I don't know if I should still take remedy from her..

[message 1000171]
Oh! Thank you so much!
Dad's completely well again!

[message 1000172]
And Sella's all right too!
It's wonderful!

[message 1000173]
Well met.
You look a fine sort.

[message 1000174]
Someone like you might...
No, never mind...

[message 1000175]
This is Wren. She's one of the elves.
Things between humans and elves are touchy,
but the two of us get on well enough.

[message 1000176]
Be happy.
Nothing matters more.

[message 1000177]
....

[message 1000178]
I'm sorry,
but I'd rather be alone..

[message 1000179]
So the army really is on the move.
The forest may be closed off again.

[message 1000180]
Aldric and I fought monsters side by side at the main front.

[message 1000181]
Humans and elves have long kept apart,
but fighting together, we might get past
what divides us...

[message 1000182]
Yet the two peoples still drift apart.
Some folk won't give us the time of day...

[message 1000183]
Together, nothing could stand against us.

[message 1000184]
I hear the fever's getting worse. The elven remedy
treats it well, and the herb should be
growing in that garden...

[message 1000185]
Not enough remedy!?
The herbs have done well this year.
Odd...

[message 1000186]
I've heard bad things about the man
who keeps the herb garden.

[message 1000187]
It may only be envy, since he's rich,
but something could be going on...

[message 1000188]
....

[message 1000189]
What?
The keeper of the herb garden..?

[message 1000190]
So that's why the remedy costs so much. It's shameful.
Elves and humans worked so well together on that garden.

[message 1000191]
But if mistrust keeps growing,
things between elves and humans will only get worse.
Someone has to act.

[message 1000192]
......

[message 1000193]
We could go to Faelan, the elf ranger who keeps watch over
the Forest of Silence, south-west of town.
He may know what to do!

[message 1000194]
He's an elf who values friendship with humans,
and he has friends on both sides, so he may help set
this right. Will you go and talk to him?

[message 1000195]
The Forest of Silence lies south-west of this town.
Watch your map so you don't lose your way.

[message 1000196]
You did it! Wonderful. Most people would never have
managed what you've been through, but you're not most people!

[message 1000197]
You can do what
others can't.

[message 1000198]
We won't lose heart.
Thank you so much!

[message 1000199]
Ah, I've heard a great deal about you.
A pleasure.

[message 1000200]
I'm Morrow. I see to the guards hereabouts.
Heh heh heh...
Do make friends with everyone.

[message 1000201]
Heh heh heh...

[message 1000202]
The remedy?
Yes, we grow the herbs for it here.

[message 1000203]
I gather it's been a poor year
for the herbs.

[message 1000204]
I only command the guards, you understand.
Any questions, put them to the steward...

[message 1000205]
The steward, an elf, is away somewhere distant just now.
You'll find him hard to reach.
...Heh heh heh.

[message 1000206]
I think you ought
to grow up a little...

[message 1000207]
Well? What is it?
Been listening to ugly gossip about me?

[message 1000208]
Now, now, calm yourself.
Yes, I have made more money than most.

[message 1000209]
That comes of hard work and heaven's favor.
Heaven sees how hard I work, and to give thanks
I made a generous gift to the temple.

[message 1000210]
The priest was most grateful.
Not bad, eh?
None of you could make the faithful
smile like that.

[message 1000211]
I give of my own wealth because my heart is pure.
A greedy man would never do such a thing.

[message 1000212]
What's more, I've already been cleared.
An official inspector found me blameless.

[message 1000213]
So if you doubt me, you doubt the kingdom,
the king and heaven itself.
Think about that.

[message 1000214]
Though it's probably wasted breath,
telling all this to a sword-for-hire...

[message 1000215]
Had you been born into money,
you'd have a better life
than one of blades and spells.

[message 1000216]
Even once you've paid for your sins in the world below,
you'd do well to pray
to heaven.

[message 1000217]
You've nothing to offer heaven,
so I'd say you'd better pray hard!

[message 1000218]
Mwa ha ha..

[message 1000219]
Ha ha ha!

[message 1000220]
What's the matter with you?
Have you no shame?

[message 1000221]
Heaven chose me.
You chose wrongly...

[message 1000222]
Thrown out of the Guild and barred from trading?!
And a prison sentence???

[message 1000223]
Lies! This is a cruel joke...
I have deals under way!

[message 1000224]
And what about my debts?

[message 1000225]
You! Why in the world would you do this...

[message 1000226]
Oh, I see it now!

[message 1000227]
Very well, how much? How much do you want?

[message 1000228]
It's money, isn't it? You're jealous that heaven favors me.
This is too much!

[message 1000229]
You've no idea how much money passes through my hands!
More than ordinary folk
earn in all their lives!

[message 1000230]
If it's money you want, just say so.
Why treat me so cruelly?

[message 1000231]
Don't care for my manner?
Then I'll pay you even more.

[message 1000232]
Enough to live at your ease for good!
What do you say? Wouldn't that be nice?
Never work another day. Imagine it!

[message 1000233]
No common soul could ever live like that.
It's what every ordinary person dreams of,
and I'll make it real for you! There! How about that?

[message 1000234]
But you must save me! Tell them I'm innocent!
Saving me is worth more to you than saving
a thousand nobodies! Can't you see that?

[message 1000235]
Curse it... I can't stand fools...

[message 1000236]
Oh....

[message 1000237]
Ruined... I'm ruined... What will become of me?

[message 1000238]
Name's Hask. I'm a smith,
and fine work is my trade.

[message 1000239]
I can make your gear like new! And how
about a new color for your equipment?

[message 1000240]
Heh heh heh...
I've good things for sale.

