[message 1000000]
Forest of Silence

[message 1000001]
You're new around here, aren't you? Well met.
I'm Faelan. I range these woods for the elves.

[message 1000002]
The humans in these parts keep their word.
When they fell trees, they take only what
they agreed to and spare the rest.

[message 1000003]
Because they're careful, elves and humans can
share this land in peace. I'd ask you to
remember that.

[message 1000004]
Lately, though, monsters are tearing the forest
apart, and I can't see how we'll stop them...

[message 1000005]
Anyway, I'd be grateful if you looked after
the forest too, from here on.

[message 1000006]
Hello. We've no answer to the monsters here.
Whatever you do, stay clear of the worst of it.

[message 1000007]
Our forest...
Nothing hurts like seeing it torn up.

[message 1000008]
Ah, news from Wren!
Morrow's dealings have made me uneasy
more than once.

[message 1000009]
It seems he's thrown in with crooked nobles
who line their pockets, and this time he's
gone much too far.

[message 1000010]
I've already told some honest nobles and the
merchants' guild. If a proper inquiry looks
into that garden, the truth will come out.

[message 1000011]
There's one trouble, though.

[message 1000012]
Some elves who have no love for humans will
try to use this for their own ends.

[message 1000013]
They'll say humans can't be trusted anymore.
They might demand payment, or demand that
the humans quit the forest altogether.

[message 1000014]
Those elves keep their standing by stirring up
hatred. They meddle in everything and tangle
every matter they touch.

[message 1000015]
We mustn't throw away a bond that took
so many years to build.

[message 1000016]
This forest has done well because humans
and elves have been friends.

[message 1000017]
...If you've the time someday, I'll tell
you more about it.

[message 1000018]
Anyway...

[message 1000019]
Things are going badly, and I have a plan.
It may sound reckless. Will you at least
hear me out?

[message 1000020]
Not long ago, savage giant spiders moved into the
Forest of Silence. They can ruin these woods, and
rangers have already died trying to kill them.

[message 1000021]
We're afraid they'll multiply, yet we elves
can do nothing about them.

[message 1000022]
Humans could deal with them, though. You fight
them better than we do. Clear them out, and
the trouble is over.

[message 1000023]
Sir Aldric tells me you're a fine fighter.
It won't be easy, but will you help us?
Think it over, please.

[message 1000024]
Sir Aldric and Wren rarely speak that well of
anyone. Now that I've met you, I can see why.

[message 1000025]
You're back! I feared I'd sent you to your death.
I'm so glad you wiped them out.

[message 1000026]
Thanks to you, the Forest of Silence can heal
and be quiet again. You have my deepest thanks!

[message 1000027]
And there's more good news!

[message 1000028]
Morrow's crooked trading and his deals with
the bad nobles are out in the open. He was
hiding a store of medicine.

[message 1000029]
The garden's owner has agreed to hand the
medicine out to all, so the fever should
soon lose its grip.

[message 1000030]
Well,
Morrow won't be trading again for some time
after this.

[message 1000031]
Nor will anyone want to deal with him; he's
brought shame on elves everywhere.

[message 1000032]
They say he may be ruined, too. He sank
every coin he had into herbs.

[message 1000033]
Greed blinded him, and now he's paying for it.
A sorry man.

[message 1000034]
From now on, we'll put him to honest work
with his hands, same as us!

Ha ha ha!

[message 1000035]
Hello there! How are things?

