[message 1000000]
Fanann, Village of Elves

[message 1000001]
Fanann, Village of Elves

[message 1000002]
Hello there. I'm Corvin; this post is mine
to run now. Glad to have you.

[message 1000003]
Good news: the elves have finally agreed and
given us leave. You can go back to surveying
the Mining Tunnel of Yugunos for us.

[message 1000004]
For the Mining Tunnel of Yugunos, head southwest
from Butterfly Hill and take the mountain path
they call the Dragon Road.

[message 1000005]
I'm relying on you.

[message 1000006]
And keep clear of the seal works if you can.
We need the elves to go on trusting us...

[message 1000007]
Just as I feared. The seal works are broken,
and the way to the deep end of the tunnel is shut.
The dragons will wake; it's only a matter of when.

[message 1000008]
To strengthen the seal on the dragons, Sylvar wants
the Power Supply Facility taken back from the demons.
It lies past the Labyrinth of Mauve, a long way
south of the elves' village.

[message 1000009]
Set out for the facility right away.

[message 1000010]
The Power Supply Facility is far to the south.
Good luck out there!

[message 1000011]
Nicely done. Here's what you've earned.
My thanks.

[message 1000012]
Sylvar may have told you already. What comes
next is about as hard a job as they come.

[message 1000013]
Slay the dragons of legend!

[message 1000014]
Do as Sylvar says: pour power into the seal first
and the dragons will be weakened for a while.
Then, and only then, you might stand a chance.

[message 1000015]
If you hold back, know that the seal will fail
sooner or later regardless.
It's a cruel thing to have to choose.

[message 1000016]
...If you walk away, nobody will hold it
against you. It's your call.

[message 1000017]
Everything's underway.

[message 1000018]
You're a true hero; people will speak of this
for a long time. Thank you, truly!

[message 1000019]
The pay isn't much this time,
I'm afraid, but you have our
deepest respect.

[message 1000020]
You ought to go to the central front next.
After what you've done here, they'll give
you a warm welcome.

[message 1000021]
And I'll make sure they know I back you
without reservation.

[message 1000022]
These days nobody faces dragons for glory.
They're all too frightened.

[message 1000023]
Who you are and what drives you, I can't say.
But I'm sure you could change this world.

[message 1000024]
The world needs someone like you.

[message 1000025]
In any case, thank you for all of it.
Go and get some rest.

[message 1000026]
Every day at the central front they fight battles
that could decide the world. You might be the one
who tips the scales. There's something about you.

[message 1000027]
If your road goes on from here, I'd be glad
if it led you that way...

[message 1000028]
Latest word: our surprise strike worked, but the
enemy is holding hard. Our soldiers are worn out,
and they need you to take over for them.

[message 1000029]
So make for the Yugunos camp. The Warp Gate
will get you there quickly.

[message 1000030]
All the best to you.

[message 1000031]
Be welcome.
I am Edda, elder of this forest.

[message 1000032]
Orsolan has told me everything. We will help
the army's work in whatever way we can.

[message 1000033]
But the seal on the dragons must be handled
with great care. Something is coming that
none of us can escape...

[message 1000034]
Go well.

[message 1000035]
How goes your survey?

[message 1000036]
I can hardly take it in.
The dragons are truly dead?

[message 1000037]
We thought we would live out our days crouched
beneath the fear of those beasts. You have
lifted that weight from all of us.

[message 1000038]
I have no words equal to this. Thank you,
from all my heart! Our people will gladly
work with the army again.

[message 1000039]
Our history has a new hero in it,
and we have gained a dear friend.

[message 1000040]
May heaven watch over you!

[message 1000041]
The Moonwell Tear, gem of the king of the
spirits? So you know of it?

[message 1000042]
Well...
Ever since someone stole the Moonwell Tear,
there has been nothing but trouble.

[message 1000043]
Shall we win it back?

[message 1000044]
Oh yes, returning it to the one it belongs
to would surely bring you a reward.

[message 1000045]
The Moonwell Tear!!

[message 1000046]
The Dark Elves had it?
...Some of us had our suspicions.

[message 1000047]
I never truly thought you would recover it...
For this, you may make use of Big Warehouse V.

[message 1000048]
Hello. I'm Sylvar. I share the watch over
the seal works that hold the dragons.

[message 1000049]
Thieves raided the seal works, and now they
are in peril. Part of the emergency defenses
has already switched on.

[message 1000050]
Go with great care.

[message 1000051]
Tell me if you discover anything.

[message 1000052]
Is there a sealed-off spot on B2F of the
Mining Tunnel of Yugunos?

[message 1000053]
Then the automatic emergency defense may be on.
Shutting it off means reaching the control room
through the underground passage that runs south
of the Mining Tunnel of Yugunos.

[message 1000054]
The trouble is, monsters have taken over that
passage, so we can't get near the control room.

[message 1000055]
Could you clear those monsters out, so we can
reach the control room?

[message 1000056]
You've taken the control room back, I see.
I'll begin shutting down the emergency defense.

[message 1000057]
The way should be open all the way to the
emergency defense itself.

[message 1000058]
So that's how it is. The seal works are badly
damaged. I'm afraid nothing can stop the
dragons from rising again now.

[message 1000059]
They say the Dark Elves smashed some of the
warding walls, so the seal must be far weaker
than it was.

[message 1000060]
The dragons will tear through the seal
on their own and get free...

[message 1000061]
...

[message 1000062]
And then this land will burn to ash, just as
Orsolan's homeland did...

[message 1000063]
No!
They have to be stopped!

[message 1000064]
I've heard what you can do. Will you hear a request?

[message 1000065]
Will you fight the dragons?

[message 1000066]
It's a wild plan, I know, but there is a chance.
If every bit of our power goes into the seal,
the dragons won't be able to fight at
full strength...

[message 1000067]
And someone as skilled as you might truly bring
them down.

[message 1000068]
We will not get another chance.
Please, help us!
Talk it over with your commander first if you wish.

[message 1000069]
I know that battling the dragons sounds
like madness, but there is no other way
left to us...

[message 1000070]
Now we will pour every scrap of our power
into the seal.

[message 1000071]
All I can do is make the seal stronger and
the dragons weaker...

[message 1000072]
Heavens...

[message 1000073]
Someone who can actually slay the dragons...
I can scarcely believe it. Forgive me for laying
so much on you. And thank you, truly!

[message 1000074]
What a foolish thing
I've done...

[message 1000075]
I paid my daughter no mind, and now she
has run away!

[message 1000076]
I carry the proud name of Tallow, yet I could
not even make my only daughter happy!

[message 1000077]
I put the customs of this house before
what she felt.

[message 1000078]
Lissa! Oh, Lissa... Is she safe?
I can't stop worrying...

[message 1000079]
Oh! It's you. You gave me a fright...
Might I ask something of you?

[message 1000080]
Please find my Lissa.

[message 1000081]
I'd wager she's hiding at Dr. Holt's workshop,
east of here. She must be set against the match
I arranged with the Marsh family.

[message 1000082]
Tell her that if she comes home, she may
do whatever she likes.

[message 1000083]
And give Dr. Holt my thanks. We have
put him to a great deal of bother.

[message 1000084]
I beg you.
I'm counting on you.

[message 1000085]
Good luck to you!

[message 1000086]
Thank you for going. What a relief to hear
that Lissa is well.

[message 1000087]
But why does she say she needs more time?
What is she up to?

[message 1000088]
Hmm...

[message 1000089]
I know! Your name has reached me, and I know you
are busy, but with skills like yours, I would
ask one more thing of you...

[message 1000090]
Would you help Lissa with
whatever it is she means to do?

[message 1000091]
Your reward, paid ahead. Please take it.

[message 1000092]
Keep Lissa safe...

[message 1000093]
So. My son walked into the trap, just as I
feared he would. It was bound to happen.

[message 1000094]
Perhaps we slighted the honor of the elves.
We should never have let Marsh deal with
the Dark Elves.

[message 1000095]
Marsh's meddling has brought us to ruin...

[message 1000096]
Help us, please.
Put an end to Marsh's wicked schemes!

[message 1000097]
As an elf, I feel bound to set right what
Marsh has done wrong. Please!

[message 1000098]
I can never thank you enough... So many elves
were caught up in this mess, and you saw
us through it.

[message 1000099]
A small gift for you. Please accept it.

[message 1000100]
Thank you so much for all your help!
My son and daughter both seem to have grown
up a little through all of this.

[message 1000101]
We lost a great deal, but what we
gained is worth more.

[message 1000102]
Thank you for everything.

[message 1000103]
Safe travels to you.
And thank you, once more.

[message 1000104]
Rubbish! Why would my father ask you for help?
It's people like you who make everyone sneer at me!
He's dragged the Tallow name through the mud!

[message 1000105]
And you're what, a warrior? Don't make me laugh!
Are you mocking me!?

[message 1000106]
Get out of here, you vermin!
Look down on me once more and
I'll kill you!

[message 1000107]
Idiot! I am... I am!

[message 1000108]
Curse it. Why can't I ever measure up
to my father...

[message 1000109]
Nothing eats at me more than how far I
fall short of my father.

[message 1000110]
Why?

[message 1000111]
...Ah, forgive me.
That was rude of me.
......

[message 1000112]
The spirit teachings will be lost, and it'll
be my fault. Curse it!

[message 1000113]
...I see. If Dr. Holt thinks so, I'll do as he says.
I'm only a piece on the board here.

[message 1000114]
Thank you for everything. Because of you,
I might find my feet again. Such sure eyes...
I was an elf ranger once, and I respect
the strength I see in you.

[message 1000115]
I need to sharpen my own skills.

[message 1000116]
Anyway, I'll ask my old elf ranger friends
and see how I can help you.

[message 1000117]
And if you can, tell Lissa not to push
herself so hard!

[message 1000118]
My father and Lissa are
both fretting over me...
They still think I'm a child.

[message 1000119]
....
Lissa really does seem to be
working herself hard... (sigh)

[message 1000120]
Oh, the elf rangers say they've turned up
something worth knowing. I've already
passed it along to Dr. Holt.

[message 1000121]
I've got my hands full,
so I asked Dr. Holt to
write it up for you.

[message 1000122]
I hear Marsh has done something crooked...
Will you help me bring his misdeeds to light?
Go talk it over with Dr. Holt, please.

[message 1000123]
Meeting you makes me want to take up
the sword and the bow again...

[message 1000124]
But there's other work for me now.

[message 1000125]
Truth be told, I loathe Marsh, but he's an elf
the same as me. I don't want him ruined.
Please help us.

[message 1000126]
If only we'd learned of Marsh's
crimes sooner.

[message 1000127]
Fine work! Marsh is back in the hands of the
elves. We'll see to him from here on, so don't
worry; this is our responsibility as well...

[message 1000128]
Your road ahead may be hard, but it's far
gentler than the one your enemies walk.

[message 1000129]
You've taught me a great deal. Thank you.
This is for you. Things are lean for me
just now, so it's all I can give.

[message 1000130]
I ought to study harder. As I am now, I'll
never surpass what my father has done.

[message 1000131]
I'll begin again from the start!

[message 1000132]
Dr. Holt!
How often do I have to tell you
I hate being called that?!

[message 1000133]
Dr. Holt!
I'm not a little girl anymore!
(sulking)

[message 1000134]
Oh, I'm sorry, I didn't notice you...
Wait, you're... the warrior who beat the Gargoyles!
They say Orsolan the wizard sent you here.

[message 1000135]
You look so strong!

[message 1000136]
Oh, where are my manners?
I'm Lissa. Pleased to meet you.

[message 1000137]
I'm the Tallow daughter, and I've been hiding
here. Please keep it a secret.

[message 1000138]
Father sent you to look for me?
Was he worried? I'm sorry.
I never meant to cause such a fuss...

[message 1000139]
Please tell my father
I have to stay here a while yet.
I'm not ready to come home.

[message 1000140]
Be sure he hears it, please.

[message 1000141]
You're back, good. Did my father say anything?
How did he take it?
I'm nothing but trouble...

[message 1000142]
May I ask you for something?

[message 1000143]
It's about my father, the head of the Tallows.
We fell on hard times, so he meant to borrow
a great deal of money from Ruben Marsh.

[message 1000144]
The money trouble began when the business my
brother Bram ran went under. But it seems Marsh
may have tricked him into it.

[message 1000145]
My brother is desperate to do better
than our father ever expected of him.

[message 1000146]
He never stopped trying.
Not for a single day.

[message 1000147]
While he ran the company himself, all was well.
But once he let some of our father's old kin
mind it in his place. He trusted them.

[message 1000148]
That's when the debts started piling up. Someone
was borrowing in the company's name. The man in
charge back then vanished, and our money with him.

[message 1000149]
He'd also spent that money buying up other
companies at outrageous prices. And every one of
them, it turned out, was buried in debt...

[message 1000150]
Father paid back what he could, but it wasn't
nearly enough. In the end he went to Ruben Marsh,
his old rival, for a loan.

[message 1000151]
Marsh named a hard price for it.
He wants this coal mine for himself.

[message 1000152]
In his hands, the spirit teachings are fading.
We've held them sacred for generations,
and we're fighting to keep them alive.

[message 1000153]
Marsh promised to leave the teachings alone
if I married his son. Father said yes.
He actually agreed to it!
I still can't believe it.

[message 1000154]
And of course, I have no wish at all
to become the wife of Marsh's son.

[message 1000155]
I barely know the man. Besides, I want to look
further into this loan of Marsh's.

[message 1000156]
Dr. Holt is helping me with it, so I need
to stay out here a little while longer.

[message 1000157]
If you could lend us a hand with all this,
I'd be so grateful.

[message 1000158]
Please, help us.

[message 1000159]
Please. I'm begging you.

[message 1000160]
Oh? My brother says I shouldn't work too hard?
Then tell him the very same from me.

[message 1000161]
Thank you for carrying our words back and forth.
My brother must take you for a messenger bird.

[message 1000162]
Don't take that the wrong way. Now then...
Oh, that's right! By now my brother ought to
have heard something from the elf rangers!

[message 1000163]
Thank you so much. My brother was so low,
but thanks to you he's finding his feet again.

[message 1000164]
You're more than I hoped for... When we met,
I thought you might be of some help.
Now I know I can trust you with anything.

[message 1000165]
Amazing!
How could anyone pull that off?
I could never do what you do!

[message 1000166]
Thank you for everything.
You're so brave.

[message 1000167]
I ought to try much harder myself.
I must tell Dr. Holt that... Oh, never mind!

[message 1000168]
Hee hee... (she blushes)

[message 1000169]
Keep lending a hand to those who need one.
I'll try to do the same!

[message 1000170]
Heh heh heh... How long I've waited for this.
The last days of the Tallows.

[message 1000171]
Soon all they own will pass to the Marsh family.

[message 1000172]
All my years of bitterness are nearly over.
The Tallows will answer to a Marsh!

[message 1000173]
The spirit teachings? Nothing but a pretty
excuse for filling their purses.

[message 1000174]
I, Ruben Marsh, will show that coward Tallow
how a mine should be run!

[message 1000175]
Those teachings turn my stomach! If it's money
we want, we sell this town's precious ore cheap.
That would keep our old buyers happy...

[message 1000176]
I'm not joking!
There is only peace when the strong
keep the weak firmly under heel!

[message 1000177]
Tallow's soft hand has brought
nothing but quarrels!

[message 1000178]
Once I've made this mine mighty,
everyone will see what I'm worth.

[message 1000179]
...Heh heh. Perhaps I'll give a good fright to
those country folk who tried to drive us out...

[message 1000180]
They're in my grip now.
You'll see. The final blow is coming soon!

[message 1000181]
No! My plans!
Curse you, Tallow!

[message 1000182]
This isn't over...
One day I'll have my revenge!

[message 1000183]
Who's this? A human, aren't you?

[message 1000184]
How curious that lowly beasts like you
have any brains at all.

[message 1000185]
I am Ewan Marsh, the future lord
of these lands!

[message 1000186]
Kneel before me!
No?
You beasts never understand anything.

[message 1000187]
You're good for nothing. Perhaps it would be
best to wipe out your worthless kind
altogether, wouldn't it?

[message 1000188]
You most of all.
I don't like the look in your eyes.

[message 1000189]
When this business is over, you'll be the
first one I ask my father to have killed.

[message 1000190]
Let me explain something to you.
At the top of the world there is a god, and
we elves of the Marsh family stand one step
beneath.

[message 1000191]
Slave elves like the Tallows
are far, far below us.

[message 1000192]
And far below even them are the humans.

[message 1000193]
Understand? That's how this world is ordered.
You exist to follow.
Heh heh heh! (he puffs up with pride)

[message 1000194]
Though I should mind my tongue in front
of humans, however stupid they are.
(he smirks)

[message 1000195]
Father, crush the Tallows at once.
I can't wait a moment longer!

[message 1000196]
Lissa will soon be my bride.
Ha ha ha!

[message 1000197]
Lissa has run away from home!?
Such a lovely little thing.

[message 1000198]
Heh heh... Once we're wed, I'll give her
plenty of reasons to cry.
Father, I can't wait any longer!

[message 1000199]
Father, I'm out of patience!
Fetch Lissa back this instant!
And my birthday present had better be
twice as big as last year's!

[message 1000200]
What? What's happening!?
What do my servants think they're doing!

[message 1000201]
They never dared even meet my eyes!

[message 1000202]
Where did they find the nerve to stone me? Ow!
I'm bleeding! Curse them! I should have strung
more of them up from the trees while I could!

[message 1000203]
Just you wait! My father will round you all up,
and then we'll have our revenge. No more mercy
from me! Heh heh heh...

[message 1000204]
What?
My father's been arrested?

[message 1000205]
Nonsense!
That can't be true!

[message 1000206]
What's the matter with all of you?
Stop looking at me like that!
So we dealt with Dark Elves. What of it?
Is that so terrible?

[message 1000207]
My father isn't like you. He's great! A noble elf
can do as he pleases! You're only jealous
because you're poor! Isn't that it?
Say it!

[message 1000208]
Why?
Why won't anyone listen to me?
This is madness...

[message 1000209]
Father... Please...
Save me...
Father!

[message 1000210]
Have you heard? The great elf families of
this forest are at each other's throats.

[message 1000211]
The Tallows against the Marsh family.
I can hardly wait to see who comes out on top!

[message 1000212]
The Tallows have always come out ahead before.
The Marsh family is a nasty lot,
and nobody thinks much of them.

[message 1000213]
Plenty of folk stand by Tallow, since his family
keeps the spirit teachings.

[message 1000214]
They say a Tallow ancestor found this mine,
led here by the spirits. Is it true there's
all kinds of rare ore down there?

[message 1000215]
Being so famous, the family keeps to itself.
There's a lot of mystery about them.

[message 1000216]
The Tallows and the Marsh family couldn't seem
more different.

[message 1000217]
Tallow has kept the family name strong for
years. But his heir Bram keeps making big
mistakes, and lately he's in real trouble.

[message 1000218]
I'd hate to see the Marsh family beat the Tallows.

[message 1000219]
Oh, and there's talk that Tallow's
daughter Lissa has gone missing.

[message 1000220]
Everyone thinks she's hiding at Dr. Holt's
laboratory. They say the two of them
are rather close.

[message 1000221]
Dr. Holt is the finest engineer there is.
He knows how to refine magic crystals.

[message 1000222]
He's human, but Lissa doesn't mind that one
bit. She looks up to him. Who knows, someday
they might... (she smiles knowingly)

[message 1000223]
I wish I had a sweetheart like that.

[message 1000224]
Have you heard? Marsh's secret trade with the
Dark Elves has come out! And the swindle he ran
on Tallow too. There's no escaping it now.

[message 1000225]
The elf who ran Bram's company into the ground
has been arrested too. Tallow's luck has turned.

[message 1000226]
Things will be a bit dull now the Marsh family
can't put up a fight anymore.

[message 1000227]
Well, it won't stay quiet for long. Tallow
doesn't have the mine all to himself, so
others may jump at the chance.

[message 1000228]
What's going to happen next? I can't wait!

[message 1000229]
Oh, dear. What am I to do?

[message 1000230]
Lissa.
I'm worried about you.
Your father must be beside himself
now that you've run away.

[message 1000231]
Allow me to introduce myself. I'm Dr. Holt.
We study ways to refine the ore that comes
out of this mine.

[message 1000232]
The Tallow mountains around here are rich in
precious ore, but people never stop
fighting over it...

[message 1000233]
This time the Marsh family got the upper hand.
To keep the mountains in Tallow hands, Lissa
was promised to the Marsh boy.

[message 1000234]
I know how she feels. Not that I wanted
to marry her myself, of course...

[message 1000235]
In any case, Lissa, your family
must be worried sick about you!

[message 1000236]
I never knew Lissa thought so deeply...
She's grown into a woman so fast.

[message 1000237]
Don't stare at me like that, Lissa.
You aren't a little girl anymore.

[message 1000238]
Lissa and her moods...

[message 1000239]
At any rate, I've been looking into Marsh too.
I spoke with our lab workers and with
the people who buy our crystals.

[message 1000240]
Ugly rumors about Marsh have been
going around for a while.

[message 1000241]
To an elf, trading in secret with Dark Elves
is like selling your soul to a devil.

[message 1000242]
Most likely Marsh began the secret trade
so as not to miss the fortune this war offers,
and to pay for his feud with Tallow.

[message 1000243]
A fight with Tallow would have cost
him a great deal of money.

[message 1000244]
Dark Elves...

[message 1000245]
Of course! I've heard that Lissa's brother
was once an elf ranger, and fought
the Dark Elves more than once.

[message 1000246]
His friends among the rangers might be able
to tell him something about the Dark Elves.

[message 1000247]
Please, would you go to him and
tell him what we've talked about?

[message 1000248]
I'm sorry to trouble you so much.
I'll do some digging of my own as well.

[message 1000249]
Thank you. With what you've brought us,
there's no longer any doubt: Marsh is trading
with the Dark Elves in secret.

[message 1000250]
Whenever anyone smelled a scandal,
he found a way to bury it...

[message 1000251]
But at last we have hard evidence. Goods from
his Dark Elf deals are hoarded at a small shrine
to the west, perhaps disguised as ordinary stock.

[message 1000252]
Forbidden drugs, banned weapons,
magic equipment and the like.

[message 1000253]
If we can lay hands on those goods,
we can prove what Marsh has been doing.

[message 1000254]
If the powerful elves grow closer to the
Dark Elves, this land will sink into
violence and drugs.

[message 1000255]
They must be stopped, but our army and the
elf rangers are tied up with the war. They've
no time to spare for smugglers like these.

[message 1000256]
And if they get mixed up in it, Marsh's
friends will get in the way of our inquiry.

[message 1000257]
So I'm turning to you. Nobody here knows you,
but the allied army and the wizard Orsolan
both vouch for your skill and character.

[message 1000258]
Only you can act here without
falling under Marsh's sway.

[message 1000259]
No one else can bring Marsh's
crimes into the light.

[message 1000260]
So here is my request. The Marsh family's hidden
storehouse lies at the far end of the Forest of
Wesley, past the northwest side of Butterfly Hill.
Go there and lay their secret trade bare.

[message 1000261]
It's a hard task, but we truly need you.

[message 1000262]
You did it! With this evidence we can finally
bring charges. Marsh has nowhere left to run!

[message 1000263]
You're everything they say you are!
You beat the Dark Elf guards! Thank you so much.
My laboratory will be safe now too,
all thanks to you.

[message 1000264]
You really are as skilled
as everyone says.

[message 1000265]
Hello.
We refine ore here and study it.

[message 1000266]
Dr. Holt's refining methods are wonderful.
We use them on tools for Orsolan
and other wizards.

[message 1000267]
Tallow is a good man.
He'll hire anyone, human or elf,
it makes no difference to him.

[message 1000268]
I'd guess that's because
he trusts Dr. Holt.

[message 1000269]
If the Marsh family ever took over here...
(he shudders)
I'd rather not think about it.

[message 1000270]
Marsh is greedy. He drives
his workers into the ground.

[message 1000271]
"The rich are loved by the gods; everyone else
is a slave." That's how Marsh excuses himself.

[message 1000272]
Anyone who complains gets punished,
and he shows no mercy.

[message 1000273]
To someone like me, it's a frightening thing.

[message 1000274]
Hello, I've heard of you. You're the one who
uncovered Marsh's secret trade.
Well done!

[message 1000275]
What I still don't see is why Tallow didn't
simply do away with Marsh. Why take
the long road?

[message 1000276]
Is it the spirit teachings? I live by them
too, but I can't see why they matter
so much to him.

[message 1000277]
Maybe I'd understand if I rose higher in the world.

[message 1000278]
Looking to buy? Or shall I repair
or identify something for you?

  ~Buy weapons           ~
  ~Buy gear              ~
  ~Identify items        ~
  ~Repair items          ~
                              ~Leave~

[message 1000279]
  ~Weapon             %9d Gold~
  ~Helmet             %9d Gold~
  ~Body armor         %9d Gold~
  ~Shield             %9d Gold~
  ~Boots              %9d Gold~
  ~Everything worn    %9d Gold~
  ~Everything carried %9d Gold~
                          ~Leave~

[message 1000280]
Looks like you're a bit short of gold.

[message 1000281]
That doesn't need any repair.

[message 1000282]
Identifying it costs %d Gold. All right?

                         ~Yes~  ~No~

[message 1000283]
You don't have anything unidentified.

[message 1000284]
The name's Bramble.
I keep a shop here in town.

[message 1000285]
I wasn't sure I could make a living selling to
elves, but now that I know them, I find
they're not so different from us humans.

[message 1000286]
I'm Fennel, a spirit healer.

[message 1000287]
If you're hurt or worn out,
come and see me.

[message 1000288]
Your companions are welcome too.

[message 1000289]
Spirits!
Mend their wounds!

[message 1000290]
There, you're well again.

[message 1000291]
Heh heh heh...
I've got some fine wares.

