[message 1000000]
Tower of Licarn, 5F

[message 1000001]
I am Licarn, a holy knight.
You'd be the sellsword Lissa told me about, yes?

[message 1000002]
You've come to hear how the elven rangers
were wiped out. Am I right?

[message 1000003]
In truth, it was Lord Valdric who set off the chain
of events that ended in that disaster.

[message 1000004]
He asked the elven rangers to look into the thefts
of holy relics that have been going on of late.

[message 1000005]
They were the finest rangers there were, yet they
were ambushed and slain while they searched.
Lord Valdric is half human and half elf, and now
the elves lay the blame at his feet.

[message 1000006]
And the timing of it all tells me someone inside
the church is working hand in hand with the enemy.

[message 1000007]
Wait... What's this?

[message 1000008]
......

[message 1000009]
Odd...
The tower has stopped working.

[message 1000010]
Give me a moment.

[message 1000011]
.......

[message 1000012]
I thought so.
Someone outside is working the tower...

[message 1000013]
With the transport down, nobody can move between
the floors. Someone has to go down to the first floor.

[message 1000014]
I haven't the gear to fight my way down there.
Would you go in my place?

[message 1000015]
Reaching the first floor may be enough to set
the tower running again. If it does, come back
and see me.

[message 1000016]
You can't transport straight up to a higher floor.
And the warp runes between the floors only go
one way. Mind yourself.

[message 1000017]
Take care.

[message 1000018]
My thanks.
Who would do such a thing, I wonder...

[message 1000019]
......

[message 1000020]
Ah, yes... the rangers and the stolen relics.

[message 1000021]
Does the name Gorr mean anything to you?

[message 1000022]
No, I didn't think so.
Long ago there was a holy knight called Gorr.

[message 1000023]
A fine knight, until the day he dared to question
the ways of the grimling faith. That was forbidden...

[message 1000024]
I'll spare you the whole tale for now, but
the grimlings put him to death as a traitor.

[message 1000025]
You're wondering what that has to do with the thefts?

[message 1000026]
Just before the relics began to vanish, a grave
keeper found Gorr's tomb empty. His body was gone.

[message 1000027]
So the holy knights whisper among themselves that
Gorr has risen to take his revenge on the grimlings.

[message 1000028]
That's all I know.
I hope it's of some use to you.

[message 1000029]
Why would I help you, you ask?

[message 1000030]
Ha ha ha.
An old friend of mine in the mining town
told me all about you.

[message 1000031]
I can feel a power in you that might change the world.
See that you use it for the good of us all.
Now, go on with your journey.

