[message 1000000]
A Town of Antalusia

[message 1000001]
A Town of Antalusia

[message 1000002]
I am Aurel, a bishop of the grimling faith.
Yours is a face I don't know.

[message 1000003]
Hm? A letter for me,
from Rector Rowan?

[message 1000004]
Give it here...

[message 1000005]
...

[message 1000006]
I see how things stand.
Nobody has any business training in that tower.

[message 1000007]
Carry a note with my seal on it,
and no one there will stand in your way.

[message 1000008]
I trust you to see this through.

[message 1000009]
I trust you to see this through.

[message 1000010]
The Sacred Feather! A holy relic
of Valmere, back in our hands!

[message 1000011]
You have our thanks for bringing it home.
You shall have a reward.

[message 1000012]
A fighter for hire would rather have something
useful than a fine title, I imagine.

[message 1000013]
...

[message 1000014]
Let me think...

[message 1000015]
Would the use of Big Warehouse III, in the Proving
Tower at Cold Svalt, suit you?

[message 1000016]
Valmere watch over you!

[message 1000017]
The demon army keeps reaching for Valmere's holy
relics. It is madness, and it is happening everywhere.

[message 1000018]
There have always been thieves, but lately the
strange happenings come thicker and faster...

[message 1000019]
We had only just learned that a relic lies in a cave
beneath one of our churches, and at once demons moved
in and took the cave.

[message 1000020]
That is far too neat to be chance.

[message 1000021]
By bringing back the Sacred Feather you have earned
our trust. So I would ask one more thing of you...

[message 1000022]
Clear every demon out of that cave beneath the church,
and bring back the relic called the Angel's Tress.

[message 1000023]
The way down into the cave
is at the back of this church.

[message 1000024]
You have courage to spare,
slayer of the dragon.

[message 1000025]
I leave it in your hands.

[message 1000026]
I leave it in your hands.

[message 1000027]
There it is! The holy relic of Valmere.
We are deeply in your debt!

[message 1000028]
In thanks, I will teach you one of the old
spells our faith has kept secret all these years.

[message 1000029]
  ~Hell Fire        ~  A blast of fire all around you.
  ~Ice Blast        ~  Pillars of ice rise around you.
  ~Heal             ~  Brings your strength back.
  ~Earth Spears     ~  Spears of earth strike the foe.
  ~Sonic Blade      ~  Sends out cutting shock waves.

  ~Experience instead~  50%

[message 1000030]
That spell is one you already know, it seems.

[message 1000031]
Use this power from now on to keep the world safe.

[message 1000032]
Use this power from now on to keep the world safe.

[message 1000033]
You brought back two holy relics.
I could not ask for better proof of your worth.

[message 1000034]
Whenever there is work, we will call on you first.
Have no fear, the army has agreed to it.

[message 1000035]
There is something only a few grimlings know.
I will share it with you, but keep it to yourself.

[message 1000036]
Our faith honors Valmere, the White Angel. We hold
that her holy relics are the key to the magic and
might of the Ancient World.

[message 1000037]
Long ago, people misused that ancient power,
and it poisoned the world.

[message 1000038]
The east suffered worst of all. The land was ruined,
and no one could live there without machines
to clean the air.

[message 1000039]
If that power ever reached the wrong hands, our world
would be lost. It is frail now, and what strength we
have today could never hold such a threat back.

[message 1000040]
So the grimlings of old hid Valmere's relics and
scattered them to every corner of the world.
Now it falls to us to seal them away once more.

[message 1000041]
Some of our sealing works, the dragon seal in the
Yugunos mining tunnel and the Proving Tower among
them, were built to hold ancient beings. Some of us
would put them to use, some would not. But enough.

[message 1000042]
Now, about these recent thefts of the relics...

[message 1000043]
The latest was in the cave beneath our church, just
as we learned the relic was there. That cannot be luck.
We believe one of our own grimlings has
very likely betrayed us.

[message 1000044]
So we wanted someone the grimlings don't know
to look into it. That is why we turned to you.

[message 1000045]
Will you go to our fort at Losmans and
give this report to Lord Valdric?

[message 1000046]
Losmans lies far to the west. Go through this town
and on through Gungstonwald, then keep heading west.
The road is long, but you will get there.

[message 1000047]
The fate of the world may rest with you.
Don't lose heart.

[message 1000048]
What's this?
They won't let you into Losmans while the castle
wall is under repair?

[message 1000049]
The wall at Losmans draws its strength from the
light of the Ancient World. I hear that strength
has been failing since the last great attack.

[message 1000050]
General Brannoc lives here in town. He may
know more about what is happening at Losmans.

[message 1000051]
Would you go and speak with him?

[message 1000052]
Thank you.

[message 1000053]
Well? Are you buying or not?

  ~Buy weapons           ~
  ~Buy gear              ~
  ~Identify items        ~
  ~Repair items          ~
                              ~Leave~

[message 1000054]
  ~Weapon             %9d Gold~
  ~Helmet             %9d Gold~
  ~Body armor         %9d Gold~
  ~Shield             %9d Gold~
  ~Boots              %9d Gold~
  ~Everything worn    %9d Gold~
  ~Everything carried %9d Gold~
                          ~Leave~

[message 1000055]
You can't afford that.

[message 1000056]
Nothing here needs mending.

[message 1000057]
Identifying that comes to %d Gold. All right?

                         ~Yes~  ~No~

[message 1000058]
There's nothing unknown here.

[message 1000059]
I'm Tamsin.
I carry goods you won't see
anywhere in the east.

[message 1000060]
Care for an affinity tonic?
Drink one and you can change your attributes
however you like.

[message 1000061]
Want your old attributes back? Then drink the
clearing tonic. It isn't cheap, mind.

[message 1000062]
You can only drink one of each affinity tonic.
And you can't hand them to anyone else; in the
wrong hands they'd be dangerous.

[message 1000063]
Once you've bought one, pick SPECIAL ITEMS
on your item screen, or press X to open
the special items window.

[message 1000064]
Well, what's keeping you?

[message 1000065]
I'm Ilse.
A spirit healer now, and a dancer once.

[message 1000066]
Did you know a spirit healer
has to be able to dance well?

[message 1000067]
There! Not bad, am I?

[message 1000068]
My dance can mend your wounds.
Watch!

[message 1000069]
My dance is only for
those who are hurt.

[message 1000070]
...

[message 1000071]
So you're the fighter Bishop Aurel spoke of.
I am General Brannoc. Keeping Antalusia
and its roads safe is my charge.

[message 1000072]
This is about the castle wall at Losmans, then.

[message 1000073]
The last attack drained most of the wall's power.
The works are unsteady while they mend it, so no one
is being let into the town.

[message 1000074]
The army means to feed the wall from another
power works and bring it back to strength,
but...

[message 1000075]
the demons have taken that works,
and there's the trouble.

[message 1000076]
It sits in the Remains of Heartbeat, in the Wilds of
Ryumyaku, north of West Antalusia and east of the
Plain of Dialose. Will you go there and
win the works back from them?

[message 1000077]
I'm grateful for your help.
Give it all you have.

[message 1000078]
So you've won back the Remains of Heartbeat.

[message 1000079]
Fine work, and my thanks.
You know your trade well.

[message 1000080]
I'd like to tell you the wall is safe now,
but the reports say things have only grown
more tangled.

[message 1000081]
The Remains of Heartbeat had been idle as a power
works. Someone appears to have taken over the pipe
works that carry its power on to Losmans.

[message 1000082]
From what I hear, the demons treat
those pipe works like a shrine.

[message 1000083]
Doesn't it strike you as odd how the demons
keep turning up in just the right places?

[message 1000084]
Look into those pipe works for me. They stand
by the Gulf of Lucentia, west of the Plain of
Dialose and north of West Antalusia,
south of the town of Calado.

[message 1000085]
You're better than
most swords for hire.
Keep it up.

[message 1000086]
Keep it up.

[message 1000087]
My thanks.
Take this for your trouble.

[message 1000088]
Word is the castle wall at Losmans is mended.
Another attack as big as the last shouldn't
come soon. For now, we're safe.

[message 1000089]
You'll be making for Losmans.
The lands west of it are dangerous,
so keep your guard up.

[message 1000090]
With Aurion close by, the demons of the west are
fiercer than those of the east. Don't think too much
of yourself, and be ready for what lives there.

[message 1000091]
Will peace ever come?

[message 1000092]
Have you heard?
They say the Moonwell Tear, the gem of
the king of the spirits, was stolen!

[message 1000093]
Have you heard?
There's a sword for hire out there getting
back the Moonwell Tear, the gem of
the elves' king of the spirits!

[message 1000094]
Hm? Can I help you?

[message 1000095]
I hear there's an apple tree
down in South Antalusia.

[message 1000096]
Apples aren't for me.

[message 1000097]
Curse it! With demons all around here
I can't go out and gather fruit.

[message 1000098]
Here's a tip for you.

[message 1000099]
Green apples grow
on the Plain of Dialose.

[message 1000100]
The demons keep me
from leaving town.

[message 1000101]
Oh, I heard something...

[message 1000102]
There's a merchant selling meat
in Gore Cave, out in Gungstonwald.

[message 1000103]
Hm? What is it?

[message 1000104]
Grandpa once brought a fruit
back from Gungstonwald.
It was so good.

[message 1000105]
Plumvine fruit, wasn't it?

[message 1000106]
Mmm...

[message 1000107]
A bit of pepperfire sauce
right now... mmm...

[message 1000108]
Hey, wait!?

[message 1000109]
That... that's pepperfire sauce!?
Where did you find it?

[message 1000110]
Say, would you let me have it?
I'll trade you something rare for it.

[message 1000111]
Calado lies northwest of this town, Losmans
to the west, and Ponse, Village of Dwarves,
to the southwest.

[message 1000112]
And who might you be?

[message 1000113]
Heh heh heh...

[message 1000114]
Pay me 80,000 Gold and I'll let you in on something.
Well?
                    ~Yes~  ~No~

[message 1000115]
Suit yourself. You're a fighter after all.

[message 1000116]
Heh heh... You're quite something.

[message 1000117]
Step onto the Warp Gate to travel.

[message 1000118]
Keep at it.

[message 1000119]
You haven't got the gold.

[message 1000120]
Step right up!
I've some mighty fine goods.

