[message 1000000]
Town of Losmans

[message 1000001]
Town of Losmans

[message 1000002]
What a mess this all is...

[message 1000003]
...

[message 1000004]
Yes? What brings you here?

[message 1000005]
My lord, you mean to hear out
some stranger off the road?

[message 1000006]
And why not? Road dust aside,
this one looks honest enough.

[message 1000007]
Wait... you carry a report
from Bishop Aurel of Antalusia?

[message 1000008]
Hand it here.

[message 1000009]
Now then...
So, this concerns the sacred relics.

[message 1000010]
If I read it right, you are the one
who brought two of them back to us.

[message 1000011]
Hm...

[message 1000012]
It bears his seal; it is genuine.
You have my thanks. Take this as a sign of it.

[message 1000013]
We are still looking into who stole them.

[message 1000014]
Tell me, would you serve at my side,
as my own sword?

[message 1000015]
My lord, call me the moment
anything seems amiss.

[message 1000016]
Well... what I need from you
is that you keep me safe.

[message 1000017]
As you command.

[message 1000018]
So, what do you say?

[message 1000019]
Bishop Aurel writes that you
know how to handle yourself.

[message 1000020]
Is that so?

[message 1000021]
You answer to no one, it seems. And anyone
who hands stolen relics back instead of
selling them must be someone I can trust.

[message 1000022]
Someone like you is exactly what we need.
Things have been tense around the grimling
faith of late.

[message 1000023]
Which is why I never leave Lord Valdric's side.

[message 1000024]
There is one more thing, but it stays
between the two of us. Understood?

[message 1000025]
Breathe a word of it to anyone,
and you won't live to regret it.

[message 1000026]
Petrus, enough!

[message 1000027]
Forgive me, my lord.

[message 1000028]
Where was I... Not long ago I sent our
elf rangers out to track down the relics.

[message 1000029]
Then they vanished without a word,
and soon after we found every one dead.

[message 1000030]
They could have brought down the Ancient Dragon
had they tried. I doubt men or a pack of
demons did this; something else was at work.

[message 1000031]
I want you to find out what it was.

[message 1000032]
I will let the town's leading folk know
who you are, so no one wonders about you.

[message 1000033]
I am relying on you.

[message 1000034]
I am relying on you.

[message 1000035]
Ah, you've come at just the right moment.
A report from Archbishop Krator
arrived only a little while ago.

[message 1000036]
He has found a relic, the Silver Spike.
It lies in a Dragon Cave in the Forest of
Ilbarna, to the west of South Losmans.

[message 1000037]
The dragons there are asleep, so taking it
should be simple. Go and bring it back. You
slew the Ancient Dragon; if they wake, so be it.

[message 1000038]
I would go myself, were I not
already sworn to my post.

[message 1000039]
I look for great things from you.

[message 1000040]
I look for great things from you.

[message 1000041]
Well, look at that!
The Silver Spike itself.
You've done it!

[message 1000042]
...

[message 1000043]
The dragons woke?

[message 1000044]
Archbishop Krator's report said
they were sound asleep...

[message 1000045]
Still, you put them down, did you not?
Beating those on top of the Ancient Dragon...
you are a fighter to be reckoned with.

[message 1000046]
And I missed all of it...

[message 1000047]
Here is your reward,
with my thanks for a job well done.

[message 1000048]
I expect only the best from you.

[message 1000049]
Archbishop Krator is studying the ruins
on the Hill of Heaven, you say?

[message 1000050]
No one told me of that.

[message 1000051]
This smells wrong. Would you go
and find out what he is up to there?

[message 1000052]
Show my letter and they will let you in.
The ruins sit on the Hill of Heaven,
north of the Forest of Ilbarna.

[message 1000053]
My lord, about those ruins...
aren't they the ones where...

[message 1000054]
Yes, those. Some old power down there stops
any warp from working; you can't travel out
by magic once inside.
Take care.

[message 1000055]
Stay strong.

[message 1000056]
Someone is digging up the old world's
knowledge in the Ancient Ruins?

[message 1000057]
And Gorr the traitor was with them?

[message 1000058]
Then Archbishop Krator may well be...

[message 1000059]
Ah... I...

[message 1000060]
My lord, what is it?

[message 1000061]
Can't... get... my breath...

[message 1000062]
Poison?!
Did Archbishop Krator put
something in that wine?!

[message 1000063]
...

[message 1000064]
You there!
Get him an antidote, quickly!
I'll do what I can to hold it back.

[message 1000065]
The dwarves of Ponse make a cure for any
poison. Their village lies to the southeast!

[message 1000066]
Ponse is east across the Moldona Peninsula,
which runs out from South Losmans.
Go, and hurry!

[message 1000067]
(Gasp)

[message 1000068]
(Swallows)...

[message 1000069]
...

[message 1000070]
...

[message 1000071]
...(Breathes hard)

[message 1000072]
My lord!
How do you feel?

[message 1000073]
I think...
I will... pull through.

[message 1000074]
Thank the gods...
I owe you more than I can say this time.

[message 1000075]
Could Archbishop Krator truly
be behind this...?

[message 1000076]
Take this for your trouble.
I am more grateful than words allow.

[message 1000077]
Hm...

[message 1000078]
What?
Archbishop Krator's own servant told you so?

[message 1000079]
Hm...

[message 1000080]
This has gone too far already.
We must weigh our next step with great care.

[message 1000081]
...

[message 1000082]
My lord, should you tell them?

[message 1000083]
I will...
But this must stay a secret.

[message 1000084]
Krator once had a son, and a gifted one.

[message 1000085]
Some years back, he and I were both
put forward to become cardinal.

[message 1000086]
The choice fell on me, because my mixed blood
let me win the trust of elves and men alike.

[message 1000087]
Krator took it hard back then,
but in the end he bowed to it.

[message 1000088]
And then... came the trouble...

[message 1000089]
Let me tell it, my lord.

[message 1000090]
Not long after Lord Valdric took office,
the demons grew bold, and the army was sent
out to meet them.

[message 1000091]
Battle followed battle, and the men
were soon worn to the bone.

[message 1000092]
That was when disaster came...

[message 1000093]
Krator's son took a company out to strike
the enemy, but word went astray and the elf
rangers never came to back them up.

[message 1000094]
The demons cut them down to the last man,
the archbishop's son among them.

[message 1000095]
When Krator heard the news, someone
overheard what he said...

[message 1000096]
He claimed the elf rangers had left his son
to die on purpose, on Lord Valdric's orders.

[message 1000097]
There is no truth in it at all. Orders got
lost, and the soldiers were simply spent.

[message 1000098]
Since that day Krator has buried himself
in the study of the relics, and he is not
the man he once was.

[message 1000099]
I fear he means to strike back at me and the
grimling faith with some power of the old world.

[message 1000100]
In any case, take this for all you've done.

[message 1000101]
Word has reached us that Archbishop Krator
has shut himself away in the Remains of the
Dead, in Alteria, far off to the west.

[message 1000102]
We are rooting out his helpers among our own
people, but that will be slow work.

[message 1000103]
So I ask you to make for
the Remains of the Dead.

[message 1000104]
Head east over the Hill of Heaven, follow the
Road of Atonement and pass by Sena's Small Shrine
to reach Alteria. I'll send word to the shrine.

[message 1000105]
They say Krator now commands a dark power from
the old world. Stop him; we are counting on you.

[message 1000106]
...

[message 1000107]
I am relying on you.

[message 1000108]
I am relying on you.

[message 1000109]
Splendid work.
Though it is a sad end for Archbishop Krator...

[message 1000110]
Take 100,000 gold, and with it
the use of Big Warehouse IV, as my thanks.

[message 1000111]
You have saved the grimling faith. From now
on, every ruin we hold is open to you.

[message 1000112]
My lord, is that wise?

[message 1000113]
It is.
There may yet be things down there
that can help.

[message 1000114]
Go where you will.

[message 1000115]
I am deeply grateful.

[message 1000116]
I've heard tell of gold and silver orbs
hidden in some of those ruins.

[message 1000117]
You are always welcome here.

[message 1000118]
I have a favor to ask.

[message 1000119]
Do you know of the wild lands northwest of
Calado? No one may go in there any longer.

[message 1000120]
We sealed them off, for the demons there keep
growing stronger. But a party that searched
the place brought us word of Valmere's relics.

[message 1000121]
We believe the White Locket, a relic of Valmere,
lies in an old research hall in the Wyrmwood.
Go by the Ruins of the Lake, west of Calado.
Would you bring the relic back to me?

[message 1000122]
Those wild lands west of Calado
lie under the magic of Aurion.

[message 1000123]
Watch yourself. The demons
out there are far stronger.

[message 1000124]
We are counting on you.

[message 1000125]
Valmere's relic!
You have my thanks. And here is the reward
I am sure you have been waiting for.

[message 1000126]
Hm?

[message 1000127]
Saint Seren...?

[message 1000128]
Very well...
I will tell you something of her.

[message 1000129]
As you surely know, we grimlings
hold Valmere, the White Angel, sacred.

[message 1000130]
Our teaching says Valmere is the angel
who locked the devil Morvane away in Aurion.

[message 1000131]
When she founded our faith, she left us two
lessons: how to live on in this tainted
world, and how to bring Morvane down
should he ever return.

[message 1000132]
We held to them. To keep the world from
further harm we turned to the old world's
craft, and so we began digging in the ruins.

[message 1000133]
In one of them we found a girl asleep inside
a glass tube full of liquid.
We gave her the name Seren.

[message 1000134]
You want to know what she has
to do with Valmere, I expect.

[message 1000135]
Her tube bore an inscription,
carved into its side.

[message 1000136]
"Within sleeps Valmere born again.
She shall wake when the world draws to its end."

[message 1000137]
And then, to our amazement, she woke. She
remembered nothing, and spoke and acted
like any other girl.

[message 1000138]
The demons have grown steadily for two years;
surely that is what woke her. And if she has
risen, Morvane is likely back as well.

[message 1000139]
That is why we dig for Valmere's relics.
We are making ready to fight him.

[message 1000140]
There is one more thing I would ask of you.

[message 1000141]
Take the sacred relics we have gathered
and bring them to Saint Seren.

[message 1000142]
She may strike you as an ordinary girl.
Never forget what binds her to Valmere.

[message 1000143]
You have my thanks.

[message 1000144]
You have my thanks.

[message 1000145]
So you have met her. Hard to believe
that Saint Seren is Valmere reborn, isn't it?

[message 1000146]
From this day on, I ask that you serve
Saint Seren, which is to say, Valmere's own will.

[message 1000147]
Go west past West Calado and through the
Labyrinth of the Lake. Berini Village lies beyond.

[message 1000148]
The world's fate rests with you now.
All of us are counting on you.

[message 1000149]
Well now!
Are those collector's gems you're carrying!?

[message 1000150]
Garnet,
diopside,
lapis lazuli...

[message 1000151]
Morganite,
kyanite,
chiastolite...

[message 1000152]
Hessonite,
amethyst,
and rose quartz...

[message 1000153]
Every last one of them...

[message 1000154]
What a treat to see. In return,
let me tell you something few people know.

[message 1000155]
Over the years we have put down
a great many demons.

[message 1000156]
Some, though, were far too strong for us.
The most we could manage was to seal them away.

[message 1000157]
If you want to test yourself against
something truly fearsome, go where they are held.

[message 1000158]
The Warp Point will take you to that
hidden place.

[message 1000159]
Such a fine collection. I'm jealous.

[message 1000160]
Good heavens! You destroyed the demons
we never dared to face?

[message 1000161]
Is there anything left in this world
that could stand against you?

[message 1000162]
At this rate there won't be a demon left
anywhere. Splendid work!

[message 1000163]
A hired sword likes a solid reward, I expect.
Giant Warehouse X is yours to use from now on.

[message 1000164]
May your strength always be spent
for the good of all people.

[message 1000165]
Buying, or do you need something
repaired or identified?

  ~Buy weapons           ~
  ~Buy gear              ~
  ~Identify items        ~
  ~Repair items          ~
                              ~Leave~

[message 1000166]
  ~Weapon             %9d Gold~
  ~Helmet             %9d Gold~
  ~Body armor         %9d Gold~
  ~Shield             %9d Gold~
  ~Boots              %9d Gold~
  ~Everything worn    %9d Gold~
  ~Everything carried %9d Gold~
                          ~Leave~

[message 1000167]
You don't have the money for that.

[message 1000168]
Nothing here needs any work.

[message 1000169]
Identifying that will cost %d Gold. All right?

                         ~Yes~  ~No~

[message 1000170]
You've got nothing that needs identifying.

[message 1000171]
Name's Ewart.
A town with a castle, I figured there'd be
folk like me in Losmans.

[message 1000172]
Turns out I figured wrong.
It's all fine lords and ladies around here...

[message 1000173]
I'm Clara, a witch who serves
the holy spirits.

[message 1000174]
They told me Losmans was always bustling,
but it's so quiet... Maybe the last attack
scared folk off. I miss the crowds.

[message 1000175]
Drop by whenever you like.

[message 1000176]
Spirits of light,
mend what evil has torn!

[message 1000177]
You're in good shape.

[message 1000178]
...

[message 1000179]
I am here to keep
Lord Valdric safe.

[message 1000180]
Don't stand around. Get going!

[message 1000181]
You've done fine work.

[message 1000182]
I have something you should hear.

[message 1000183]
A few bishops have shut themselves up in a tower
in the Golas Desert. It ties back to Krator's plot.

[message 1000184]
They may be harmless, but
we can't simply leave them there.

[message 1000185]
Destroy the phantoms that guard the tower,
and they will likely scatter.

[message 1000186]
What happened to Krator's son was a mistake.
No one means to punish them. Could you
talk them out of their thirst for revenge?

[message 1000187]
The Warp Rune will take you to the tower.
I'm relying on you.

[message 1000188]
Well done. This is your reward.

[message 1000189]
At last we can all rest a little easier.

[message 1000190]
Here, let me pass along
something worth knowing.

[message 1000191]
There are nine kinds of collector's gems.
Gathering all of them is no small task:
they cost a fortune, and when a monster
drops one it can be lost for good.

[message 1000192]
Lord Valdric has long had a keen eye
for collector's gems.

[message 1000193]
And who might you be?
I am Ambrose the Mighty.
Were you speaking to me?

[message 1000194]
A hired sword?
Your kind has no business here.

[message 1000195]
Slack off, and folk around here will
call you a coin-grabber.

[message 1000196]
Me? Oh, I'm quite safe.
I am mighty, and my presence is precious.
They cannot do without me.

[message 1000197]
Run along back to your
little errands.

[message 1000198]
Archbishop Krator!? What are you saying?
That cannot be true!

[message 1000199]
It's all over... I'm ruined...

[message 1000200]
Good day.
I am Sir Linus.
And you are?

[message 1000201]
Ah, the hired sword. That last attack
was a hard one, wasn't it?
Thank you for all you did.

[message 1000202]
I may be a noble, but I try to live
like anyone else.

[message 1000203]
Nobles are little better than thieves. We are
paid for doing nothing. Some thieves at least work.

[message 1000204]
Why so many nobles think themselves
above others, I'll never understand.

[message 1000205]
Ambrose over there is the worst of them.
Pay him no mind.

[message 1000206]
Thank you.
Keep up the good work.

[message 1000207]
So you're the hired sword
Lord Valdric spoke of.

[message 1000208]
You've heard what became of the elf rangers?
I can't say what happened, but I have
a friend who is a holy knight.

[message 1000209]
He might know things about it that
no one else does.

[message 1000210]
His name is Licarn.
He keeps a tower in
South Losmans.

[message 1000211]
I'll send word to him.
Pay him a visit when you can.

[message 1000212]
Thank you.
Good luck to you.

[message 1000213]
Archbishop Krator did all that?
I can scarcely believe it!

[message 1000214]
Ambrose must be crushed.

[message 1000215]
Archbishop Krator was the one
who backed him.

[message 1000216]
Pride always comes down a peg in the end.

[message 1000217]
I am Warrick, servant and steward
to Archbishop Krator.

[message 1000218]
My master is away.

[message 1000219]
My master is away.

[message 1000220]
You... came back alive?

[message 1000221]
Oh, it's nothing.

[message 1000222]
I hardly think my master's whereabouts
are any concern of yours.

[message 1000223]
Very well, very well. My master is at the
Hill of Heaven, studying the sacred relics.

[message 1000224]
Kindly leave him in peace.

[message 1000225]
Kindly leave him in peace.

[message 1000226]
What?! ... The truth, is it?
You truly want to hear it? Then listen...

[message 1000227]
It was all our doing! The raid on Losmans,
the slaughter of the elf rangers,
the stolen sacred relics...

[message 1000228]
And why?

[message 1000229]
Because of the grimlings
and Lord Valdric, that's why!

[message 1000230]
And now you know everything,
and still there's nothing you can do.

[message 1000231]
Our one mistake was that you didn't
die in the Dragon Cave.

[message 1000232]
Archbishop Krator holds every advantage.
Victory is ours!

[message 1000233]
I have only to see Lord Valdric poisoned and
my task is finished. Let them catch me and
hang me, for all I care.

[message 1000234]
Hahahaha.

[message 1000235]
Ha ha ha ha.

[message 1000236]
Dead?! No, it can't be! No!
I won't believe it...

[message 1000237]
Pardon me, and who are you?

[message 1000238]
A hired sword, is it? I am the lady
of this house. You may call me Mrs. Rowan.

[message 1000239]
You hire out your services, yes?
Might I ask a favor of you?

[message 1000240]
I love to sew my own dresses, but there's
no decent material to be had in this town.

[message 1000241]
Would you be so kind as to find me some
white cloth, red thread and a silver needle?

[message 1000242]
Any of the other towns should have them
for sale, I'd think.

[message 1000243]
You'll be well paid for your trouble.

[message 1000244]
Oh, you found them for me!

[message 1000245]
Thank you so much.
Please take this for your trouble.

[message 1000246]
At last I can start on a new dress.

[message 1000247]
Who are you?

[message 1000248]
Oh, the hired sword.
Here's something you might like to know.

[message 1000249]
They say a very rare medicine is hidden in
the Wham ruins, in the Mesrald Burial Grounds.

[message 1000250]
Goodness, who are you?

[message 1000251]
There's a story going around that the Silver Orb,
one of the keys to Aurion's gate, lies in
the Ruins of Lukuna out in the Golas Desert.

[message 1000252]
Though who would ever want
to go to Aurion?

[message 1000253]
Who are you?

[message 1000254]
Ah, it's you. I've heard
the tales about you. Quite something.

[message 1000255]
Here's something for you... I heard
the Gold Orb is in the Ruins of Zeres,
down on Lunafuld Beach.

[message 1000256]
?

[message 1000257]
I really want some brightfruit...

[message 1000258]
It grows along the Road of Atonement.

[message 1000259]
Hmm...

[message 1000260]
If only I had a mandrake...
Hmm...

[message 1000261]
Well, well!

[message 1000262]
A mandrake! Where did you find that?
Never mind, it doesn't matter.

[message 1000263]
Let me have it, and I'll give you
something hard to come by.

[message 1000264]
Welcome to my class. I train those
who wish to take up a new calling.

[message 1000265]
You aren't ready for my training
just yet.

[message 1000266]
Come back when you have more
experience behind you.

[message 1000267]
Very good.
You seem well seasoned.

[message 1000268]
You're ready to change your calling.

[message 1000269]
Everyone who trains here gives 100,000 Gold
to the grimlings' cause first.

[message 1000270]
Which calling would you take up?
      ~Warrior~
      ~Hunter~
      ~Wizard~

      ~Leave~

[message 1000271]
Having second thoughts?

[message 1000272]
You already follow that calling.

[message 1000273]
You don't have enough for the gift.

[message 1000274]
Very well.
We'll begin your training.

[message 1000275]
...

[message 1000276]
...

[message 1000277]
There.

[message 1000278]
Your new calling is open to you. Use the
Change Job button on your Status screen.

