[message 1000000]
Berini Village

[message 1000001]
Berini Village

[message 1000002]
I know your face.

[message 1000003]
Yes... It was you who brought
my husband down, wasn't it?

[message 1000004]
Forgive me, I never told you who I am.
I was married to Krator, who was once
the archbishop.

[message 1000005]
Don't worry. I hold nothing against you.

[message 1000006]
Losing our son to the war broke his mind.

[message 1000007]
...

[message 1000008]
...

[message 1000009]
There is one favor I'd ask of you...

[message 1000010]
We once made our home in a village west of here.
It lies in ruins now, overrun by demons.

[message 1000011]
Somewhere in those ruins is a keepsake from
our happier years. I would be so grateful
if you could bring it back to me.

[message 1000012]
It must still be lying among the ruins.
Would you go and look for it?

[message 1000013]
It must still be lying among the ruins.
Would you please find it for me?

[message 1000014]
Yes, that's the one! It's from the day my husband
and I first met. Oh, thank you so much!

[message 1000015]
Bless you. Without something of his to hold,
I don't think I could go on.

[message 1000016]
No words could ever repay you.
Please take the use of Giant Warehouse VII,
and my husband's old Mending Stone as well.

[message 1000017]
I don't really understand it myself, but they
say the Mending Stone helps wounds heal faster.

[message 1000018]
Thank you, truly, for all you've done.

[message 1000019]
Thank you, truly, for all you've done.

[message 1000020]
Well? Are you buying or just looking?

  ~Buy weapons           ~
  ~Buy gear              ~
  ~Identify items        ~
  ~Repair items          ~
                              ~Leave~

[message 1000021]
  ~Weapon             %9d Gold~
  ~Helmet             %9d Gold~
  ~Body armor         %9d Gold~
  ~Shield             %9d Gold~
  ~Boots              %9d Gold~
  ~Everything worn    %9d Gold~
  ~Everything carried %9d Gold~
                          ~Leave~

[message 1000022]
You can't afford that.

[message 1000023]
Nothing here needs mending.

[message 1000024]
Identifying that comes to %d Gold. All right?

                         ~Yes~  ~No~

[message 1000025]
You've got nothing that needs identifying.

[message 1000026]
Name's Hollis.

[message 1000027]
This place was once full of people and bustle.
Hardly anyone is left now.

[message 1000028]
Where are all these foul creatures coming from?
It isn't safe here anymore...

[message 1000029]
Go on, have a look at my wares.

[message 1000030]
I'm Edda, a witch who serves
the holy spirits.

[message 1000031]
The one before me couldn't stand this village,
so I was sent to take her place.

[message 1000032]
Holy spirits, close these wounds!

[message 1000033]
If you're ever unwell, come and find me.

[message 1000034]
Have a look, I've some fine things today!

[message 1000035]
Welcome to Berini Village.

[message 1000036]
It used to be lively here, but now...

[message 1000037]
Since Archbishop Krator died,
his widow has been heartbroken...

[message 1000038]
Oh, the late archbishop's house is just over there.

[message 1000039]
Even the woods around here have turned pale white.
They were never like this before.

[message 1000040]
Could Aurion's magic have swallowed
up the whole forest?

[message 1000041]
No one knows a thing about this tower:
when it was built, who built it, or why.

[message 1000042]
And its door is sealed shut.

[message 1000043]
Long ago, Berini Village stood west
of this town. The demons left it
in ruins.

[message 1000044]
They came without warning, and everyone
fled here to this town for safety.

[message 1000045]
South of town you'll find The Ruins of Kashugal.

[message 1000046]
I've heard the green orb is still kept
somewhere in those ruins.

[message 1000047]
Want to hear something?

[message 1000048]
I was told a wizard who knows The Ruins of The Wise
lives in a dwarf village far to the southeast!

